@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;operations] dust-dev-only
Cloud commands MUST explicitly target dust-dev. Host setup MUST verify the GCE metadata project and
allowlisted dfs-v2-spolu instance identity before mutations. Cloud resource creation and deletion
MUST remain manual user actions; setup scripts MUST NOT provision or delete cloud resources.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;operations] preserve-fdb-disks
Setup MAY format only the verified blank 375 GiB local NVMe on an allowlisted FDB node. Existing
filesystems MUST have the managed marker before reuse; unknown disks MUST fail closed. FDB MUST
require the NVMe mount and MUST NOT silently use the boot disk when that mount is absent.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;testing] networked-fdb-validation
The fixture MUST use three distinct GCP zones as FDB replication failure domains, double redundancy,
and one coordinator per zone. Tests MUST use isolated prefixes and retain normal durable commits.
Failure tests MUST restore stopped processes and MUST NOT create or delete cloud resources.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;testing] local-generated-reports
Generated JSON reports, traces, credentials, and build outputs MUST remain outside version control.
Text summaries MUST distinguish client/server restarts from database or OS cache resets.
